The Last Night Train · 末班夜车 — Paper-cut Lightbox 纸雕灯影 (PolarMotion demo)
Polargate · PolarMotion

Story, picture, score and sound are made in code in this folder. Every paper layer, the train, the stations and the end card
are drawn by src/ (Canvas2D paper layers + three.js renderer). No photos, footage or generated images are used.
The line and its stations are fiction (see FACTS.md).

Narration
- Synthetic narration, generated offline with core/tts/tts.py.

Music (written for this film, played on sampled instruments by core/audio/sampler.py)
- Piano: "Salamander Grand Piano V3" by Alexander Holm, licensed under CC BY 3.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/)
- Instruments: glockenspiel, bowed vibraphone, harp, flute, solo violin, violins, violins tremolo, violas, cellos, contrabass, piano.

Sound effects
- Procedural (core/audio/sfx.py and mix.py): snow wind, river, sea, room tone, wheel clacks, rumble, horn, brake hiss,
  lamp clicks, shimmer, tunnel whooshes, paper.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; fetched into fonts/ by tools/fonts.py, licence texts alongside)
- Cormorant Garamond — Christian Thalmann (Catharsis Fonts), https://github.com/CatharsisFonts/Cormorant
- Noto Serif SC (subset to the characters the film uses) — Adobe / Google, https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk

Picture engine
- three.js r170 (MIT), loaded from the library's node_modules.
